WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.665
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.965 --> 00:00:15.309
Unit fourteen: Rules at Home. In this unit, you will talk about rules using must, mustn't and have to.

4
00:00:16.317 --> 00:00:17.260
Rule.

5
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.551
Rule means something that tells you what you can or can't do.

6
00:00:20.851 --> 00:00:22.804
Our family has some rules.

7
00:00:23.504 --> 00:00:26.052
Your turn. Say: Rule.

8
00:00:28.752 --> 00:00:29.393
Rule.

9
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:31.094
Must.

10
00:00:31.794 --> 00:00:34.316
Must means it is very important to do this.

11
00:00:34.616 --> 00:00:36.198
You must be home before dark.

12
00:00:36.898 --> 00:00:39.353
Your turn. Say: Must.

13
00:00:42.053 --> 00:00:42.856
Must.

14
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:44.630
Mustn't.

15
00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.121
Mustn't means it is not allowed.

16
00:00:47.421 --> 00:00:49.154
You mustn't use your phone at dinner.

17
00:00:49.854 --> 00:00:52.727
Your turn. Say: Mustn't.

18
00:00:55.427 --> 00:00:56.253
Mustn't.

19
00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.065
Have to.

20
00:00:58.765 --> 00:01:01.148
Have to means it is necessary to do this.

21
00:01:01.448 --> 00:01:02.867
I have to tidy my room.

22
00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.859
Your turn. Say: Have to.

23
00:01:08.559 --> 00:01:09.561
Have to.

24
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:11.400
Chores.

25
00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.344
Chores means small jobs you do at home.

26
00:01:14.644 --> 00:01:16.364
I do my chores on Saturday.

27
00:01:17.064 --> 00:01:19.473
Your turn. Say: Chores.

28
00:01:22.173 --> 00:01:23.046
Chores.

29
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:24.958
Bedtime.

30
00:01:25.658 --> 00:01:27.936
Bedtime means the time when you go to bed.

31
00:01:28.236 --> 00:01:30.248
My bedtime is half past nine.

32
00:01:30.948 --> 00:01:34.053
Your turn. Say: Bedtime.

33
00:01:36.753 --> 00:01:37.672
Bedtime.

34
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:39.522
Allowed.

35
00:01:40.222 --> 00:01:42.558
Allowed means you have permission to do it.

36
00:01:42.858 --> 00:01:45.067
I'm allowed to watch TV after homework.

37
00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:48.953
Your turn. Say: Allowed.

38
00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:52.631
Allowed.

39
00:01:53.617 --> 00:01:54.513
Respect.

40
00:01:55.213 --> 00:01:58.455
Respect means to treat someone in a polite and kind way.

41
00:01:58.755 --> 00:02:00.441
We respect our parents.

42
00:02:01.141 --> 00:02:04.629
Your turn. Say: Respect.

43
00:02:07.329 --> 00:02:08.191
Respect.

44
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:11.148
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:11.448 --> 00:02:14.063
Sreypich, what rules do you have at home?

46
00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:17.408
I have to do my chores every day.

47
00:02:18.717 --> 00:02:20.623
Are you allowed to use your phone at night?

48
00:02:21.917 --> 00:02:24.650
No. I mustn't use my phone at bedtime.

49
00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.520
What time must you be home?

50
00:02:28.817 --> 00:02:30.572
I must be home before dark.

51
00:02:31.883 --> 00:02:34.997
Grammar focus: Must and mustn't and have to.

52
00:02:35.297 --> 00:02:38.368
I have to tidy my room. I mustn't be late.

53
00:02:38.668 --> 00:02:42.586
'Mustn't' means not allowed. 'Don't have to' means it is not necessary.

54
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:46.270
Now read and listen. Rules in My House.

55
00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.129
Every home has rules.

56
00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:51.997
I have to do my chores, like washing the dishes.

57
00:02:53.283 --> 00:02:56.084
I must be home before dark and finish my homework.

58
00:02:57.383 --> 00:02:59.383
I mustn't use my phone at bedtime.

59
00:03:00.683 --> 00:03:04.366
I'm allowed to watch TV after homework, and I respect my parents' rules.

60
00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:08.221
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:11.475
You blank use your phone at dinner. (not allowed)

62
00:03:11.775 --> 00:03:15.255
A, mustn't. B, must. C, have to.

63
00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.797
The answer is A: mustn't.

64
00:03:22.283 --> 00:03:23.981
I blank to do my chores.

65
00:03:24.281 --> 00:03:27.656
A, have. B, has. C, must.

66
00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:34.009
The answer is A: have.

67
00:03:35.517 --> 00:03:37.447
You have permission means you are blank.

68
00:03:37.747 --> 00:03:41.632
A, allowed. B, respect. C, chores.

69
00:03:45.617 --> 00:03:47.303
The answer is A: allowed.

70
00:03:48.817 --> 00:03:52.200
Now it's your turn to speak. What rules do you have at home?

71
00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:03.822
I have to help with the cooking, and I must finish my homework before I watch TV. I mustn't stay up late.

72
00:04:04.122 --> 00:04:05.680
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:06.683 --> 00:04:10.717
Great work today! You learned eight new words and must and mustn't and have to.

74
00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:14.656
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

75
00:04:14.956 --> 00:04:17.504
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:17.804 --> 00:04:20.875
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

